===============================================================================
Title: Remove the SWRL engine lib — SHACL-AF fully takes over
===============================================================================

Context:
Follow-up to the engine swap above. The SWRL IF/THEN layer had been rerouted to
run through the new SHACL-AF engine, but the old `back/core/reasoning/swrl/`
package still existed and was the real SQL/Cypher/parse/builtin implementation
the SHACL layer delegated to. This change physically removes that package so
SHACL-AF is unambiguously in charge: the proven implementation modules were
MOVED (git mv, zero rewrite) into `shacl_rules/` and renamed to SHACL-named
classes, the orchestrator `SWRLEngine` was deleted (its URI-map helper was
extracted to a standalone function), and every importer, test, baseline, and
doc was repointed. The authoring vocabulary is intentionally KEPT intact: the
`swrl_rules` data model, the `/ontology/swrl/*` REST routes, the
`ontology-business-rules.js` UI, OWL `swrl:` serialization, the `swrl:<rule>`
provenance, and the `phase="swrl"` stats key are all unchanged, so the UI and
capabilities remain identical.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/reasoning/swrl/  (DELETED)
   Removed the entire package. SWRLEngine.py + __init__.py were deleted; the
   other 7 modules were git-moved into shacl_rules/ (next item).
2. src/back/core/reasoning/shacl_rules/  (absorbed modules, renamed classes)
   - SWRLAtomPartition.py      → RuleAtomPartition.py      (RuleAtomPartition)
   - SWRLBuiltin.py            → RuleBuiltin.py            (RuleBuiltin)
   - SWRLBuiltinRegistry.py    → RuleBuiltinRegistry.py    (RuleBuiltinRegistry)
   - SWRLParser.py             → RuleExpressionParser.py   (RuleExpressionParser)
   - SWRLSQLTranslator.py      → ShaclFlatSqlBackend.py    (ShaclFlatSqlBackend)
   - SWRLFlatCypherTranslator.py → ShaclFlatCypherBackend.py (ShaclFlatCypherBackend)
   - SWRLTextCodec.py          → RuleTextCodec.py          (serialize/parse kept)
   Method signatures and SQL output are byte-for-byte unchanged (pure rename).
3. src/back/core/reasoning/shacl_rules/rule_uri_map.py  (new)
   `build_uri_map(ontology)` — extracted verbatim from the deleted
   `SWRLEngine._build_uri_map`, with the URI local-name helper inlined to avoid
   importing `back.core.w3c` at module load (prevents a new circular import).
4. src/back/core/reasoning/shacl_rules/{SwrlToShaclTranspiler,ShaclRuleEngine,
   ShaclRuleSqlTranslator}.py
   Repointed to the absorbed modules (RuleBuiltinRegistry, RuleExpressionParser,
   build_uri_map, ShaclFlatSqlBackend); dropped all references to SWRLEngine.
5. src/back/core/reasoning/__init__.py
   Rewritten to export the SHACL rule layer (ShaclRuleEngine, ShaclRule,
   ShaclRuleSqlTranslator, SwrlToShaclTranspiler, ShaclFlatSqlBackend,
   RuleBuiltin, RuleBuiltinRegistry, RuleExpressionParser, RuleAtomPartition,
   parse_swrl_text/serialize_swrl_text aliases, builtin-fn wrappers).
6. External importers repointed to shacl_rules:
   - src/back/objects/digitaltwin/quality/SqlQualityChecks.py (parser + backend)
   - src/back/objects/digitaltwin/quality/QualitySqlBuilder.py (ShaclFlatSqlBackend)
   - src/back/core/graphdb/interfaces/GraphBackend.py (ShaclFlatSqlBackend)
   - src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/Base.py (ShaclFlatSqlBackend, postgres)
   - src/back/core/graphdb/neo4j/Store.py (ShaclFlatCypherBackend)
   - src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py (RuleTextCodec serialize/parse)
   - src/back/core/reasoning/rules/DecisionTableEngine.py (docstring)
   - src/back/core/reasoning/ReasoningService.py (docstring)
   - src/back/core/graph_analysis/CohortBuilder.py (comment)
7. Tests repointed/renamed to the new classes:
   test_swrl_engine.py, test_swrl_builtin_defects.py, test_swrl_text_codec.py,
   test_business_rules.py, test_swrl_flat_cypher_translator.py,
