================================================================================
Business Rules UI — IF/THEN authoring with read-only generated SHACL-AF view
================================================================================

Context:
Following the SWRL-lib removal (SHACL-AF is now the sole rule runtime), the
Business Rules UI still exposed SWRL as the user-facing surface: a "Generated
SWRL" preview, a raw SWRL text toggle with editable antecedent/consequent
textareas, and an "Import SWRL" modal. Since transpilation is one-directional
(no SHACL-AF -> rule parser exists), the raw/text surfaces were reworked to
show the *generated SHACL-AF* read-only, and the SWRL-text import path was
removed. The visual IF/THEN graph editor remains the authoring surface.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/reasoning/shacl_rules/rule_serializer.py (new) —
   `serialize_rules_to_turtle(rules, ontology)` renders all rules as one
   combined SHACL-AF Turtle document (single shared @prefix header + one
   sh:NodeShape block per rule, `ex:` bound to the ontology base URI);
   `preview_rule_shacl(name, antecedent, consequent, ontology)` transpiles a
   single IF/THEN rule to its {turtle, construct_sparql, rule_type} views.
   Both delegate to SwrlToShaclTranspiler (read-only, one-directional).
2. src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py — replaced the SWRL text endpoints
   `GET /swrl/text`, `GET /swrl/export`, `POST /swrl/import` with
   `GET /shacl-rules/text` (combined Turtle), `GET /shacl-rules/export`
   (.ttl download, media_type text/turtle, `<name>_shacl_rules.ttl`), and
   `POST /shacl-rules/preview` (single-rule live SHACL for the editor). The
   `/swrl/{list,save,delete,validate}` CRUD endpoints are unchanged.
3. src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_business_rules.html —
   toolbar button relabelled "SHACL" (view/export generated SHACL-AF); tab
   and pane copy relabelled SWRL -> "If-Then"; the "Generated SWRL" preview
   block became "Generated SHACL rule" (font-monospace) with a new
   `swrlAdvancedNote` shown for non-representable rules; removed the raw-SWRL
   toggle + antecedent/consequent textareas; the text modal is now read-only
   "SHACL Rules" (Import button removed, textarea readonly) and the entire
   Import SWRL modal was deleted.
4. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-swrl.js — `_updateRulePane()` now
   renders the live generated SHACL into the preview via a debounced
   `POST /ontology/shacl-rules/preview`; `refreshSwrlText()`/`exportSwrl()`
   repointed to `/ontology/shacl-rules/{text,export}`; removed
   `showSwrlImportModal()`, `doSwrlImport()`, `toggleRawMode()`, `rawMode`,
   the `swrlRawToggle` listener, and all raw-textarea reads/writes.
   Non-representable rules (built-ins / negation / derived classes) now keep
   their original antecedent/consequent verbatim in internal state
   (`_nonRepresentable`, `_origAntecedent`, `_origConsequent`) so the
   read-only SHACL view never drops them on save. Editor titles relabelled
   "Add/Edit/View If-Then Rule".
5. Tests:
   - tests/units/reasoning/test_rule_serializer.py (new) — shared-header /
     one-block-per-rule, empty + None safety, single-rule preview views.
   - tests/units/api/test_routes.py — added coverage for the three new
     `/shacl-rules/*` endpoints and asserted the legacy `/swrl/text` +
     `/swrl/import` routes now 404.
   - tests/units/front/test_swrl_text_pane.py — updated contract: read-only
     modal, no import modal/helpers, text/export target `/shacl-rules/*`.
6. Local environment repair: `brew reinstall node` relinked node against the
   current simdjson soname (node wanted libsimdjson.29, installed provided
   .36), unblocking the Node-runtime frontend tests.

